@title Consumer Lag Runbook
@subtitle settlement-consumer on payments-events
@author Streaming team, Corvid Payments

## Alert thresholds

table = Severity,Lag (messages),Duration,Action; Warning,"50,000",10 minutes,Slack only; **Critical**,"150,000",5 minutes,Page on-call; **Emergency**,"1,000,000",any,Page on-call and the Streaming lead

## Triage flow

diagram triage dir=TB title="Lag triage"
triage: alert "Lag alert fires" focus
triage: running "Consumers running?"
triage: restart "Restart consumers"
triage: skew "Partition skew?"
triage: rebalance "Rebalance partitions"
triage: scale "Scale out consumers"
triage: checkdb "Check downstream DB"
triage: recover "Lag recovering"
triage: alert -> running
triage: running -> restart : no
triage: running -> skew : yes
triage: skew -> rebalance : yes
triage: skew -> scale : no
triage: restart -> recover
triage: rebalance -> recover
triage: scale -> checkdb
triage: checkdb -> recover

## Steps

1. Check the consumer pods in the `streaming` namespace.
2. Check per-partition lag.
3. If one partition holds more than 40% of the lag, treat it as skew.
4. Scale the deployment to at most 24 replicas, because the topic has 24 partitions.

!! Never reset consumer offsets to latest. Unprocessed settlements would be skipped and would have to be reconciled by hand.

! **Escalation:** if lag is still growing after 30 minutes, escalate to the Streaming lead.
